==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|seinn|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*sainaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*sainijaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/seitn/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eitn|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|seinni|seinastur}}

# [[late]], [[tardy]]{{jump|is|late|s}}
#: ''Hann hlýtur að vera kominn — hann er aldrei '''seinn'''.''
#:: He must be here already—he's never '''late'''.
#: ''Við erum orðnar '''seinar''' í tíma!''
#:: We're '''late''' for class!
# [[slow]]{{jump|is|slow|s}}

====Inflection====
{{is-decl-adj-3|s|ei|n}}

====Derived terms====
* [[orðinn seinn]]
* [[seinn að|seinn að einhverju]] (slow at something)
* [[seinn á fæti]] (to be a slow walker)
* [[seinn fyrir]] (late, behind-hand)
* [[seinn til]] (to develop late)
* [[svifaseinn]]
* [[um seinan]] (too late)

